  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 16-layer alternating HfO2/SiO2 dielectric stack on fused silica substrate under normal air incidence. Layer sequence: HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2, HfO2, SiO2 (16 finite layers total). Initialize thicknesses at quarter-wave optical thickness for 425 nm center wavelength (HfO2 nominal 53 nm, SiO2 nominal 73 nm) with ±15% uniform random noise applied to each layer. Set optimization bounds: HfO2 layers 35-120 nm, SiO2 layers 50-150 nm. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with dual-band objective: maximize mean transmittance over 1000-1700 nm and maximize mean reflectance over 300-450 nm, equal weighting. Evaluate at normal incidence, unpolarized or average of TE and TM. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates count, tightest_margin, and thicknesses_nm for all valid candidates. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 300-450 nm, 1000-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmission in 1000-1700 nm; high reflection in 300-450 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: reflection in 1000-1700 nm; transmission in 300-450 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layer count <= 30.",
